#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064049 :question/id #uuid "3ff03590-c618-5a60-b2ac-e0a20be6a8ae" :question/math-academy-id "e-377" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int 6e^x  \\textrm d x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Factoring out the constant $6$ and taking the integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int 6e^x   \\textrm d x   =6 \\int e^x  \\, \\textrm d x =6e^x +C.\n                                                                               \n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064050 :question/id #uuid "66cbcaeb-93ee-5c15-a230-e66d2fbdd761" :question/math-academy-id "e-380" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int -6(7^x) \\, \\textrm d x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor out the constant $-6.$ Then, we integrate the exponential function, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int (-6)7^x  \\, \\textrm d x   \n&= -6\\int 7^x\\,\\textrm{d}x\\\\\n&=-6 \\cdot \\dfrac{7^x}{\\ln 7} + C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064051 :question/id #uuid "90010ae5-e211-510f-b188-dc3006926d94" :question/math-academy-id "e-381" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int 5 \\cdot 9^x +3 e^x \\, \\textrm d x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Apply the sum rule and take constant factors outside the integrals. Then integrate each exponential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int \\left(5\\cdot 9^x+3e^x\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n&=5\\int 9^x\\,\\mathrm{d}x+3\\int e^x\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\n&=\\frac{5\\cdot 9^x}{\\ln 9}+3e^x+C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064056 :question/id #uuid "f1eb9fd6-8927-54e9-bb01-57dd52871d59" :question/math-academy-id "e-386" :question/problem "Calculate the indefinite integral $$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}\\textrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}\\textrm{d}x = \\arcsin (x) + C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064057 :question/id #uuid "7a798e77-3c04-51e3-adec-d695724ce450" :question/math-academy-id "e-387" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{2}{1+x^2}\\textrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+x^2}\\textrm{d}x = \\arctan{x} + C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{1+{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064058 :question/id #uuid "6ff9c057-e61a-5648-9a49-72a70f3127bc" :question/math-academy-id "e-388" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral $$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac {x^2+2}{x^2 + 1}\\,  \\textrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This integral doesn't look like one of the basic ones. However, we can manipulate the numerator a bit  to make it look more like the denominator, which reveals a more familiar expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}+2}{{x}^{2}+1} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+1+1}{{x}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+1}{{x}^{2}+1}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRemembering that\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{1}{x^2+1} \\textrm dx = \\arctan(x),\n$$\n\nwe can now calculate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+2}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (1+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x+\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064059 :question/id #uuid "81e3df9e-e5ab-57ec-9a82-149a277e94f0" :question/math-academy-id "e-3890" :question/problem "If $f'(x) = \\dfrac{5}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2 - 1}} - 2x,$ then $f(x)=$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2 - 1}} \\, \\textrm dx = \\textrm{arcsec} \\, x.\n$$\n\nThen we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{5}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}-2x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{5}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\text{arcsec}\\,(x)-2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =5\\text{arcsec}\\,(x)-{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064538 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0eba2fed-2402-502f-a903-66cd6c74f76b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284915} {:answer/id #uuid "18dae23c-d239-55e1-b30c-540dddcea243" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(5x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285008} {:answer/id #uuid "2524b70b-9d06-5871-a0dc-3f81516ac28e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285115} {:answer/id #uuid "3705a171-a53b-5ee3-b8bf-807677a1e63e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285304} {:answer/id #uuid "8b08b682-7151-5b28-b454-865156d75731" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286064}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285115} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fa818b0-e7fa-53d7-9206-1742b2136520" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287216}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c1cea40d-e47d-5293-af9b-c5f67df8a555" :question/math-academy-id "q-19090" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{-5}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{-5}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =-5\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-5\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064539 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46152cad-db26-5489-9885-4872107442fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "11arcsecx+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285429} {:answer/id #uuid "729aed06-b282-521d-acb9-4668cd5b0175" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "arcsec(11x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285842} {:answer/id #uuid "938eb1ee-7ab4-5c5a-9a1e-41f61385c5ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "arccsc(11x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286131} {:answer/id #uuid "bacc3b3a-e948-590d-a0b3-c31bb9639de6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "arcsecx+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286488} {:answer/id #uuid "cf0db5b1-a31d-566b-9b38-cd041089c3ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "11arccscx+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286666}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285429} :answer-field/id #uuid "01c584f0-c6ff-5109-ba98-24519ff2f970" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287140}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f5ca0aa8-06db-5c6f-bb07-38d950f613d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-19100" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{11}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{arcsec}\\,x.\n$$\n\nThen we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{11}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =11\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =11arcsecx+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064540 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02d1fed6-2003-5f27-aae5-10563638a94a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3x-3\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284812} {:answer/id #uuid "4a505557-0c7c-5346-91d3-f43699946a4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\,\\text{arccos}\\,x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285476} {:answer/id #uuid "857d016b-947d-51cc-a94f-504ff730be03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3x-3\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286014} {:answer/id #uuid "95a187aa-f975-58a0-836c-3c543a56e0fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\,\\text{arctan}\\,x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286147} {:answer/id #uuid "ea53131b-47dd-5ccd-bab6-9d3aa84dd5a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3x+3\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286933}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286014} :answer-field/id #uuid "18a42158-518b-5329-b494-893d421c1e55" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287191}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2a43a9d4-962c-592e-be6c-4c9a905c5e08" :question/math-academy-id "q-19102" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This integral doesn't look like one of the basic ones. However, we can manipulate the numerator a bit  to make it look more like the denominator, which reveals a more familiar expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+1} & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}+3-3}{{x}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3({x}^{2}+1)-3}{{x}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3({x}^{2}+1)}{{x}^{2}+1}-\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cancel{({x}^{2}+1)}}{\\cancel{{x}^{2}+1}}-\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =3-\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRemembering that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,\n$$\n\nwe can now calculate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3-\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\text{d}x-3\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3x-3\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064644 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a98ed7fb-13d2-5b60-b8f1-b9d92207919e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9arccscy + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061922} {:answer/id #uuid "b93867fb-42db-5acb-a68a-30005e299288" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9\\arcsin y + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061923} {:answer/id #uuid "bc8b6862-0786-544c-b2cf-72fba94f068d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9arccoty + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061924} {:answer/id #uuid "4ab2c318-2fdc-5cba-86a4-382079b54d5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9\\arccos y + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061925} {:answer/id #uuid "5e2d502c-a116-5a96-ac5d-42ee9672c359" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-9\\arcsin y + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061926}] :answer-field/id #uuid "8a353917-489d-52d8-8a7a-c95ac1ca86e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061921}] :question/id #uuid "a2ade639-fd71-59f6-bd56-8d2ae9f2fce1" :question/math-academy-id "q-2493" :question/problem "What is $$\n\\displaystyle \\int\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{1 - y^{2}}}dy\n$$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064645 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b488418c-908d-565f-9aed-96e60daf8dc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\arcsin x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061928} {:answer/id #uuid "bf90753d-a1dc-5065-b75b-7f81eb804890" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 175921860454